00:16:07,980 --> 00:16:08,810
It's done.

258
00:16:09,160 --> 00:16:13,100
Well then, allow me to show
you to your rooms, gentlemen.

259
00:16:20,580 --> 00:16:24,057
Oh man, talk about a weird town.

260
00:16:24,140 --> 00:16:29,977
Now time to hit the loo!

261
00:16:30,060 --> 00:16:34,117
I don't think it's functional.

262
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:36,197
Oh, if that's the case,

263
00:16:36,280 --> 00:16:39,297
I won't be able to use Hermit
Purple to get info on the enemy.

264
00:16:39,380 --> 00:16:40,557
Hey, Mr.

265
00:16:40,640 --> 00:16:42,657
Joestar, what's the looks like?

266
00:16:42,740 --> 00:16:44,217
My room doesn't have a bathroom.

267
00:16:44,300 --> 00:16:46,057
Is there one in here I can use?

268
00:16:46,140 --> 00:16:48,137
Perhaps the bathroom here is communal.

269
00:16:48,220 --> 00:16:50,057
Ah, of course.

270
00:16:50,140 --> 00:16:52,477
He's so carefree.

271
00:16:52,560 --> 00:16:53,497
Good grief!

272
00:16:53,580 --> 00:16:56,617
A stand user could attack at any moment.

273
00:16:56,700 --> 00:16:58,100
He should be on guard.

274
00:17:16,260 --> 00:17:19,140
So, the Joestar party
is on the third floor.

275
00:17:19,420 --> 00:17:22,596
Maybe me and my six-shooter
ought to pay them a visit.

276
00:17:23,580 --> 00:17:24,880
Ah, Hall Force.

277
00:17:25,280 --> 00:17:27,380
So you've come. That's right.

278
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:31,517
I finally managed to track those sorry
bastards as far as this creepy town.

279
00:17:31,600 --> 00:17:33,960
But finding you is surprising, Yabba.

280
00:17:34,240 --> 00:17:37,534
I didn't think you'd come all
the way out here yourself.

281
00:17:48,560 --> 00:17:50,089
What's the matter, Nyabba?

282
00:17:50,360 --> 00:17:51,889
Did I say something wrong?

283
00:17:54,380 --> 00:17:55,620
Forgive me.

284
00:17:55,820 --> 00:17:57,940
I'm just happy, whole horse.

285
00:17:58,140 --> 00:18:00,480
It means so much that you're here.

286
00:18:00,900 --> 00:18:04,140
Thank you for coming to
see this lonely old woman.

287
00:18:04,640 --> 00:18:08,420
It is so wonderful to finally see you.

288
00:18:12,600 --> 00:18:13,940
Tell me something.

289
00:18:14,240 --> 00:18:17,416
You and my son were friends,
were you not, Cold Horse?

290
00:18:17,740 --> 00:18:18,681
Were we friends?

291
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:20,380
Uh, well, I...

292
00:18:21,540 --> 00:18:23,658
Yes, we're thick as thieves, ma 'am.

293
00:18:25,120 --> 00:18:26,640
So you were close?

294
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:29,060
Yeah, we were practically brothers.

295
00:18:29,360 --> 00:18:31,957
He was a dear friend and
an excellent partner.

296
00:18:32,040 --> 00:18:33,334
What's this all about?

297
00:18:33,500 --> 00:18:36,265
You aren't acting like
yourself at all in Yoma.

298
00:18:38,160 --> 00:18:40,740
His death must weigh heavily on you.

299
00:18:40,960 --> 00:18:42,240
Will you avenge him?

300
00:18:42,380 --> 00:18:43,792
Is that why you're here?

301
00:18:44,180 --> 00:18:46,280
Yes, that's exactly it.

302
00:18:46,420 --> 00:18:50,302
I'm gonna make sure those bastards
pay for killing my best friend.

303
00:18:52,960 --> 00:18:55,400
That's exactly what I want to hear!

304
00:18:59,980 --> 00:19:03,240
Because now I can kill you
too, you filthy traitor!

305
00:19:05,660 --> 00:19:07,660
Yoma, what the hell are you doing?

306
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:17,440
Idiot, isn't it obvious?

307
00:19:17,740 --> 00:19:19,637
You abandoned him to save yourself.

308
00:19:19,720 --> 00:19:22,437
I swore I would kill you
the moment I saw you again.

309
00:19:22,520 --> 00:19:24,696
You deserve the same as the Joestars.

310
00:19:24,860 --> 00:19:28,300
How dare you call yourself his
best friend, cretin, Judas?

311
00:19:28,880 --> 00:19:30,468
Wait, you got it all wrong.

312
00:19:30,620 --> 00:19:34,385
By the time I got there, Sinnerfall
was already a goner, honest.

313
00:19:37,360 --> 00:19:41,760
You wretch, you're as unforgivable
as that bastard Polnareff.

314
00:19:41,960 --> 00:19:45,019
I'll have you die at the
hands of my stand, Justice.

315
00:19:45,840 --> 00:19:47,400
Wait, have mercy.

316
00:19:53,840 --> 00:19:57,440
Only a few have seen the
terrifying power of my stand.

317
00:19:57,760 --> 00:20:02,040
And now you will join all of
them in death, whole horse.

318
00:20:06,200 --> 00:20:07,030
Huh?

319
00:20:07,180 --> 00:20:09,537
What the hell is happening
to the blood of my arm?

320
00:20:09,620 --> 00:20:11,738
It's like it's all just evaporating.

321
00:20:17,300 --> 00:20:20,720
It made such a fine wound, did it not?

322
00:20:21,100 --> 00:20:25,120
That's right, this is justice,
a stand that's made of fog.

323
00:20:25,340 --> 00:20:31,660
Any wound my stand happens to graze,
becomes a gaming hole, and then...

324
00:20:35,320 --> 00:20:38,660
Justice wants to dance, whole horse.

325
00:20:40,400 --> 00:20:43,620
My stance fog has entered
your arm like a string,

326
00:20:43,880 --> 00:20:47,351
and now you're a helpless puppet
I can do with as I please.

327
00:20:47,720 --> 00:20:51,880
You will die by your
own hand, whole horse!

328
00:20:58,600 --> 00:20:59,720
Damn it!

329
00:21:00,720 --> 00:21:03,220
You shouldn't get so damn cocky! Emperor!

330
00:21:04,820 --> 00:21:06,960
Die, you crazy old hag!

331
00:21:12,300 --> 00:21:13,580
Justice prevails.

332
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:15,830
Huh?

333
00:21:15,913 --> 00:21:17,577
What the hell was that noise?

334
00:21:17,660 --> 00:21:19,484
Sounded like a giant explosion.

335
00:21:19,680 --> 00:21:23,092
It came from the room at the
back of the downstairs lobby.

336
00:21:28,820 --> 00:21:31,017
Is something wrong Polnareff huh?

337
00:21:31,100 --> 00:21:35,057
We heard something strange
and came to investigate.

338
00:21:35,140 --> 00:21:35,997
Same here.

339
00:21:36,080 --> 00:21:37,597
I was about to check downstairs.

340
00:21:37,680 --> 00:21:39,497
I'll look in the lobby first.

341
00:21:39,580 --> 00:21:40,997
Call me if you find anything!

342
00:21:41,080 --> 00:21:41,910
Okay.

343
00:21:50,680 --> 00:21:53,640
Your time's finally come, Ponareth.

344
00:22:11,740 --> 00:22:14,437
All the old paintings on the tomb.

345
00:22:14,520 --> 00:22:16,477
They do the sand dance, don't you know?

346
00:22:16,560 --> 00:22:18,120
If you move too quick.

347
00:22:18,760 --> 00:22:21,177
They're falling down like a domino.

348
00:22:21,260 --> 00:22:23,817
All the birds are men by the Nile.

349
00:22:23,900 --> 00:22:25,837
They've got the money on a bed.

350
00:22:25,920 --> 00:22:27,477
Called crocodiles.

351
00:22:27,560 --> 00:22:30,437
They snap their teeth on your cigarette.

352
00:22:30,520 --> 00:22:32,797
Foreign types with a hookah. I say.

353
00:22:39,020 --> 00:22:41,660
Walk like an Egyptian.

354
00:22:53,380 --> 00:22:56,437
The blonde waitresses take their trays.

355
00:22:56,520 --> 00:22:58,437
Spin around and they cross the floor.

356
00:22:58,520 --> 00:23:00,977
They've got the moves, oh, hey-oh.

357
00:23:01,060 --> 00:23:03,097
You drop your drink,
then they bring you more.

358
00:23:03,180 --> 00:23:05,737
All the school kids so sick of books.

359
00:23:05,820 --> 00:23:07,797
They're like the punk and the metal band.

360
00:23:07,880 --> 00:23:12,037
When the buzzer rings, they're
walking like an Egyptian.

361
00:23:12,120 --> 00:23:14,697
All the kids in the marketplace say.

362
00:23:14,780 --> 00:23:15,610
Walk

363
00:23:15,693 --> 00:23:22,620
like

364
00:23:22,860 --> 00:23:23,690
an Egyptian.

365
00:23:27,520 --> 00:23:30,677
He's in the bathroom, but he's
been in there for some time.

366
00:23:30,760 --> 00:23:32,237
Of course he's taking a shit.

367
00:23:32,320 --> 00:23:34,377
The bathroom is at the end of the hall.

368
00:23:34,460 --> 00:23:36,057
I thought I just heard the word toilet.

369
00:23:36,140 --> 00:23:37,787
What are you giggling about?

370
00:23:38,040 --> 00:23:40,746
Why am I always getting
ambushed in bathrooms?
